Translated Content 2:
“I returned from the cemetery, I was looking for your horse in the gorges; instead of the horse, I sadly came upon a giant among the ogres.  
He was black-cloaked, of enormous build: even now the foulness of his skin gleams in my eyes;  
big-eared, tooth-jutting, ugly, black in color;  
he stretched out his hands to me, huge hands of his own, and on his head there seemed like a mountain a darkish leather cap.  
And he said to me: Come with me, live with me, woman, I have plenty of gold and silver, I will hide nothing from you.  
I ran away, I was frightened, and the ogre followed me with a roar; the whole world shook with the thunder under his feet;  
that voice terrified me, and mountain and plain alike turned this way and that;  
I barely made it here and told you my anguish in a hoarse voice.”

Translated Content 16:
“I returned from the cemetery, I was looking for your horse in the gorges; instead of the horse, I got lost among the ogres in misery.  
There met me one in a black cloak, with a gigantic body: even now the foulness of his skin gleams in my eyes;  
big-eared, with protruding teeth, ugly, black in color; he stretched out his hands to me, huge hands of his own, and a darkish leather hat on his head looked as small as a mountain.  
Then he said to me: Come with me, live with me, woman, I have much gold and silver, I will hide nothing from you.  
I ran away, I was frightened, and the ogre followed me with a roar; the whole world shook with the thunder of his footsteps beneath him;  
this voice terrified me, and mountain and plain alike were turning upside down; I barely made it here and told you of my woe in a hoarse voice.”

