big-eared, with protruding teeth, ugly, black in color; he stretched out his hands to me, his great hands, and a darkish leather cap on his head looked as small as a mountain.  
And he said to me: Come with me, live with me, woman, I have much gold and silver, I will hide nothing from you.  
I ran away, I was frightened, and the dev followed me with a roar; the whole world shook with the thunder of his footsteps beneath him;  
that voice terrified me, and mountain and plain alike seemed to turn upside down; I barely made it here and told you my sorrow in a hoarse voice.”

Translated Content 24:
“I returned from the cemetery, I was looking for your horse in the gorges; instead of the horse, I sadly found myself among the devs.  
