big-eared, with protruding teeth, ugly, black in color; he stretched out his hands to me, his large hands, and a darkish leather hat on his head looked as if it were only a span above the mountain.  
And he said to me: Come with me, live with me, woman, I have plenty of gold and silver, I will hide nothing from you.  
I ran away, I was frightened, and the dev followed me roaring; the whole world shook with the thunder under his feet; that voice terrified me too, and the mountains and plains turned upside down in confusion;  
I barely made it here and told you of my grief in a hoarse voice.”

Translated Content 0:
XII. The army of the Khevsurs comes down, with the banner borne before it;  
they made for the cemetery, the silent dwelling of the Kists:  
let them seek their dead, gather the hero’s bones,  
and beneath the tormentors of Zviadauri dig out their eyes.

