From both sides they shoot with guns, shouting loudly;  
both sides are troubled by the fight, both are battling steadfastly.  
The bullet has drunk much blood, — it has grazed Kutchia,  
yet the Kists still do not break, they stand like a fortress tower.  
Baburauli advised the Khევსurs to go down sword against sword.  
The matter came to swords, the shield gave way for cutting a path;  
the Khევსurs have a dear treasure and spoil to defend.  
Pharo, do not lie to Gorda, you are his accomplice;  
before the Khევსurs running headlong, a cliff and a precipice stood in their way.

Translated Content 21:
They were met by the Kists’ army too, hidden at the edge of the ravine;  
they fired their guns, their carbines belted tight;  
the Khევსur boys, sprung up in arms, do not yield the road.  
From both sides they shoot with guns, shouting loudly;  
both sides are troubled by the matter, both fight steadfastly.  
The bullet has drunk much blood, — it has grazed the gorge; still the Kists do not break, they stand like a fortress tower.  
Baburauli advised the Khევსurs to go down sword against sword.  
The matter came to swords, and the shield gave way for cutting a path;  
the Khევსurs have a dear treasure and spoils to defend.  
