Translated Content 1:
Malia is swift as a bullet, cunning as a serpent;  
all of Pshav-Khevsureti worships him, finds comfort in him;  
Crowned Tamar is always the one who says of him:  
“Only let Mindia be with me, and with him the mountain folk are a people;  
however much the enemy may strive, he can do me no harm.”  

He knows the art of defeating and crushing the foe;  
if he reaches the wounded while they are still alive,  
they need not fear death.  
His unfailing remedy will heal one cut in half;  
therefore he does not diminish in war,  
for he always has a great host;  
far and wide has gone the tale of his adventures.

Translated Content 3:
Malia is swift as a bullet, cunning as a serpent;  
all of Pshav-Khevsureti reveres him, takes him as its solace;  
Crowned Tamar is ever saying this:

“Only let Mindia be with me, and with him the mountain folk are a nation;  
however hard the enemy may strive, he can do me no harm.”

He knows the stratagems by which the enemy is defeated and crushed;  
if he reaches the wounded while they are still alive, there is no need to fear death.  
His incomparable remedy heals even one cut in half;  
thus he does not diminish in war, for he always has a great host;  
far and wide has gone the tale of his adventures.

